# Keep secrets and history out of the build context entirely.
#
# The Dockerfile copies named paths rather than `COPY . .`, so nothing sensitive
# is baked into a layer today — but the whole context is still shipped to the
# daemon and the build cache, and one future `COPY . .` would turn that into a
# published secret. Excluding it here makes that mistake harmless.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt

# EXCEPT the corporate CA roots for the build. Without this the rules above
# strip deploy/ca/ out of the build context, `COPY deploy/ca/` finds an empty
# directory, and the build fails with the SAME certificate error it was meant to
# fix -- which reads as "the fix does not work" rather than "the file never
# arrived".
#
# These are public certificates, not secrets: a CA root is what a client is
# meant to already have. The rules above exist to keep PRIVATE keys and client
# certificates out of a layer, and none of those live here.
!deploy/ca/*.crt
.git
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.log
cb_admin_mcp.*.log
tests/
.github/
